  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sector emergency public health response to the Ebola, Cholera and mpox outbreaks (Nord Kivu, Sud Kivu, Kinshasa, Kasai)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to reduce the morbidity and mortality of the mpox outbreak and mitigate its impact on vulnerable populations in the provinces of South Kivu, North Kivu and Kinshasa Provinces in the Democratic Republic of Congo.
 
Specific objectives
Strengthen local capacities for detection and early notification of mpox cases allowing a rapid and targeted response.
Improve the quality of holistic care for Mpox patients and the prevention of infections in health structures and in the community.
Strengthen risk communication and engagement and participation of local affected communities and communities at risk of mpox in the adoption of protective measures including vaccination.
Ensure coordination of the multisectoral public health response against Mpox.</narrative>
  </description>
